# Local runtime state: the browser profile holds a live LinkedIn session
# cookie, and memory.json holds personal candidate data. Never commit these.
data/

# The profile belongs in data/, but someone following profile.example.md by hand
# may drop a copy at the root instead. Catch that too -- it holds a name, a
# phone number and a resume path.
/profile.md

# Per-session notes written by whatever harness is driving this repo. They are
# working scratch -- they contain the candidate's own facts, including the
# answers to visa and salary questions -- and they are not part of the project.
# `data/` is ignored for the same reason; this directory sits outside it, which
# is why it needs its own line rather than being covered by that one.
.workbuddy/

# Working notes from building this project: product specs, milestone tickets,
# audit reports and decision records. Kept here so the published tree stays
# readable, and ignored because they are written for the author rather than for
# someone using the tool.
.notes/
